  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a +10.6pp gain over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile representation is highly beneficial. However, we only have one data point for multiprofile aggregation (avgpool). The key uncertainty is whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further exploit the multi-profile structure, or whether simple averaging already captures most of the signal. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all else constant (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000), giving a clean A/B comparison against config_002. This is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it isolates a single design variable, (2) the answer directly determines whether transformer aggregation is worth the added complexity in all future multiprofile configurations (including multimodal ones), and (3) it builds on the strongest baseline we currently have, maximizing the chance of finding an improvement while still being informative if it does not."
}

